  "id": "progressive-muscular-atrophy",
  "term": "progressive muscular atrophy",
  "definition": "Progressive muscular atrophy is an incurable motor neuron disease marked by ongoing degeneration of motor neurons. It overlaps in symptoms with related conditions such as ALS and PLS and leads to muscle wasting, weakness, and fasciculations, which can progressively impair walking, speaking, swallowing, and breathing.",
